{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/pulls/45","id":4911400436,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVGFMZs8AAAABJL4F9A","html_url":"https://github.com/tachkovsa/plerni/pull/45","diff_url":"https://github.com/tachkovsa/plerni/pull/45.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tachkovsa/plerni/pull/45.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/issues/45","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/pulls/45/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/pulls/45/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/issues/45/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/statuses/ce568ce98d0f7f3abff1c6faf8eb0c55d68715e9","number":45,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"test(spike): typecheck benchmark — stress bands + drift fixtures","user":{"login":"tachkovsa","id":15120329,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTIwMzI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15120329?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa","html_url":"https://github.com/tachkovsa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tachkovsa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## What\n\nT4b (issue #10, plan §3.1 A5, R1#5). The four-band typecheck curve, the regenerate-and-diff drift gate, and the A5 skeleton in `docs/plans/2026-10-17-spike-a-report.md`.\n\n`bench:drift-gate` applies each committed `schema.sql` to the live database `spike_bench_<N>`, regenerates `database-types.ts` with the pinned kysely-codegen 0.20.0 flags, and runs `git diff --exit-code HEAD` on that interface. An interface that already differs from HEAD is refused before codegen. The gate is not a required check. This PR does not edit `.github/workflows/` or `scripts/gates/`.\n\nStress bands do not supply an ergonomics verdict and do not select a fallback. No stress target overran the ceiling, so §3.0 is not opened.\n\n## Curve\n\n[Run 39044052211](https://github.com/tachkovsa/plerni/actions/runs/39044052211) on `c94d9a92aa85a4a97e8f4fdd57ce6171b00f6239`. Confirmed from the `typecheck-benchmark` artifact and the job log. Each figure is the maximum of three repetitions. Wall and RSS maxima are independent. The ceiling is 120000 ms and 3906250 KiB, and it binds band 75 only.\n\n| Band | Corpus wall (ms) | Corpus RSS (KiB) | Baseline wall (ms) | Baseline RSS (KiB) | Runner outcome | Over ceiling |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n| 50 | 2420 | 396212 | 610 | 228384 | stress | false |\n| 75 | 3410 | 429960 | 760 | 236704 | within-ceiling | — |\n| 200 | 18130 | 769568 | 750 | 296792 | stress | false |\n| 400 | 97440 | 1356892 | 900 | 338320 | stress | false |\n\nT4b does not change the measured program. That dispatch already measured every band. This token cannot start `workflow_dispatch`.\n\n## Verification\n\nHead `ce568ce98d0f7f3abff1c6faf8eb0c55d68715e9`. Harness: `tools/harness` compose, direct port 54320. Transcripts below are from that revision.\n\n### Clean gate (exit 0)\n\n```\npnpm --filter @plerni-spike/db-invariant bench:drift-gate\n```\n\n```\ndrift-gate: migrate band 50 onto spike_bench_50\nDROP DATABASE\nCREATE DATABASE\ndrift-gate: regenerate band 50 interface\ndrift-gate: band 50 interface matches\ndrift-gate: migrate band 75 onto spike_bench_75\nDROP DATABASE\nCREATE DATABASE\ndrift-gate: regenerate band 75 interface\ndrift-gate: band 75 interface matches\ndrift-gate: migrate band 200 onto spike_bench_200\nDROP DATABASE\nCREATE DATABASE\ndrift-gate: regenerate band 200 interface\ndrift-gate: band 200 interface matches\ndrift-gate: migrate band 400 onto spike_bench_400\nDROP DATABASE\nCREATE DATABASE\ndrift-gate: regenerate band 400 interface\ndrift-gate: band 400 interface matches\ndrift-gate: ok\n```\n\n### (a) Rename an unused column (gate exit 1, fixture exit 0)\n\n```\nbash tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/drift-fixtures/rename-unused-column.sh\n```\n\n```\ndrift-gate: migrate band 50 onto spike_bench_50\nDROP DATABASE\nCREATE DATABASE\ndrift-gate: regenerate band 50 interface\ndiff --git a/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts b/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts\nindex d6a567f..f2e4756 100644\n--- a/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts\n+++ b/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts\n@@ -29,10 +29,10 @@ export type Timestamp = ColumnType<Date, Date | string, Date | string>;\n\n export interface Ent0001 {\n   amount: Numeric;\n-  created_at: Generated<Timestamp>;\n   id: string;\n   label: string;\n   note: string | null;\n+  opened_at: Generated<Timestamp>;\n   parent_id: string | null;\n   seq: Int8;\n   status: string;\ndrift-gate: band 50 committed interface drifted\nrename-unused-column: drift-gate exit 1\nrename-unused-column: gate failed closed and the tree was restored\n```\n\n### (b) SQL change without regeneration (gate exit 1, fixture exit 0)\n\n```\nbash tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/drift-fixtures/stale-after-sql-change.sh\n```\n\n```\ndrift-gate: migrate band 50 onto spike_bench_50\nDROP DATABASE\nCREATE DATABASE\ndrift-gate: regenerate band 50 interface\ndiff --git a/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts b/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts\nindex d6a567f..c009505 100644\n--- a/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts\n+++ b/tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/.artifacts/band-50/database-types.ts\n@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ export type Timestamp = ColumnType<Date, Date | string, Date | string>;\n export interface Ent0001 {\n   amount: Numeric;\n   created_at: Generated<Timestamp>;\n+  drift_marker: string | null;\n   id: string;\n   label: string;\n   note: string | null;\ndrift-gate: band 50 committed interface drifted\nstale-after-sql-change: drift-gate exit 1\nstale-after-sql-change: gate failed closed and the tree was restored\n```\n\n### Staged interface is not a match (exit 1)\n\nA staged extra line on band-50 `database-types.ts` exits 1 before migrate, and the staged line is left in place:\n\n```\ndrift-gate: band 50 interface already differs from HEAD\n```\n\n## Risk\n\nRisk level: **high**. The fixtures apply SQL to a live database (`spike_bench_<N>`).\n\n- [ ] Low risk — observed verification only\n- [ ] High risk (authz, tenancy, crypto, plugin admission, migrations, CI/gates, release credentials, policy) → review receipt covering the current revision is linked (reviewer role, evidence ID)\n\nThe receipt binds the final head and is written by a human reviewer, or by an agent from a different model family than every generator, with that separation stated. The generator does not write that attestation.\n\n## Compliance\n\n- [x] No secrets, personal data, third-party confidential info, or private tooling/model identities in the diff or metadata (AGENTS.md §0)\n- [x] Substantial AI-generated content carries `AI-assisted: yes` (human DCO sign-off is not required at the current stage)\n- [ ] New SDK capability or trust boundary → ADR linked\n\nAI-assisted: yes\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-2da94e63-92b2-5d0e-8099-8884a9f6d0f3?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cu